# Recipe Box API test requests
#
# VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension (by Huachao Mao),
# then click "Send Request" above any block below.
# Thunder Client works too: copy the method, URL and body.
#
# Start the server first: npm run dev   (or npm run stage5, stage6, ...)

@base = http://localhost:3000

### Read: every recipe
GET {{base}}/api/recipes

### Read: filter with a query string
GET {{base}}/api/recipes?tag=vegetarian&maxMinutes=30

### Read: one recipe by id
GET {{base}}/api/recipes/3

### Read: an id that does not exist (expect 404)
GET {{base}}/api/recipes/99

### Create: a good recipe (expect 201)
POST {{base}}/api/recipes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ramen",
  "cuisine": "Japanese",
  "minutes": 40,
  "tags": ["noodles"]
}

### Create: a bad recipe (expect 400 with a list of problems)
POST {{base}}/api/recipes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "minutes": "forty"
}

### Create: forgot the Content-Type header (watch what req.body becomes)
POST {{base}}/api/recipes

{ "name": "Ghost Soup", "cuisine": "Spooky", "minutes": 5 }

### Update: change one field (expect 200)
PATCH {{base}}/api/recipes/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "minutes": 45
}

### Delete (expect 204, then run it again for a 404)
DELETE {{base}}/api/recipes/4

### A route that does not exist (expect JSON 404, not an HTML page)
GET {{base}}/api/desserts
